{"product_id":"guernsey-literary-and-potato-peel-pie-society","title":"Guernsey Literary and Potato Peel Pie Society","description":"\u003cp\u003eThe letters comprising this small charming novel begin in 1946, when single, 30-something author Juliet Ashton (nom de plume Izzy Bickerstaff) writes to her publisher to say she is tired of covering the sunny side of war and its aftermath. When Guernsey farmer Dawsey Adams finds Juliet's name in a used book and invites articulate‰ÛÓand not-so-articulate‰ÛÓneighbors to write Juliet with their stories, the book's epistolary circle widens, putting Juliet back in the path of war stories. The occasionally contrived letters jump from incident to incident‰ÛÓincluding the formation of the Guernsey Literary and Potato Peel Pie Society while Guernsey was under German occupation‰ÛÓand person to person in a manner that feels disjointed. But Juliet's quips are so clever, the Guernsey inhabitants so enchanting and the small acts of heroism so vivid and moving that one forgives the authors (Shaffer died earlier this year) for not being able to settle on a single person or plot. Juliet finds in the letters not just inspiration for her next work, but also for her life‰ÛÓas will readers. (Aug.)Copyright Reed Business Information, a division of Reed Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.\u003cbr\u003e\nDimensions: 111 x 178\u003cbr\u003e\nAuthor: Mary Ann Shaffer\u003cbr\u003e\nISBN: 9780747598800\u003cbr\u003e\nFormat: Paperback\u003cbr\u003e\nPages: 248\u003c\/p\u003e","brand":"bookhero.ae","offers":[{"title":"Default Title","offer_id":45297368957081,"sku":"15RB-4-9780747598800","price":10.0,"currency_code":"AED","in_stock":true}],"thumbnail_url":"\/\/cdn.shopify.com\/s\/files\/1\/0580\/5696\/6297\/files\/GuernseyLiteraryandPotatoPeelPieSocietyMaryAnnShaffer.jpg?v=1744474641","url":"https:\/\/bookhero.ae\/products\/guernsey-literary-and-potato-peel-pie-society","provider":"Dubai - Buy Used\/Second-Hand Books - BookHero","version":"1.0","type":"link"}